  "known_limitations": [
    "Known problem 14, residual: 93.77% of PhishTank URLs contain a path against 99.93% of benign URLs. path_length, path_depth and count_slash therefore carry some source provenance as well as phishing signal, and unlike the scheme this cannot be removed without destroying the URL.",
    "host_subdomain_count uses the simple rule 'labels minus two', so a two-part public suffix such as co.uk reads one subdomain too many. A public-suffix list was rejected as an extra dependency that would have to be versioned and defended.",
    "The suspicious-word list was fixed in advance from the phishing-URL literature and contains no brand names. A list tuned by inspecting the training labels would be a fitted parameter, and it would not transfer to the brands attacked next year.",
    "These features describe the URL string only. Nothing is resolved over the network -- no WHOIS age, no DNS record, no page content -- because PhishTank lists only currently-online phishes, so a lookup made today would describe a different internet from the one the snapshot captured."
  ]
}